If you work backwards Claude 3.5 Sonnet is only 8% failures while ChatGPR-4o is 25% worse at 10% overall failures. That is a significant change.. This view is probably the correct way to view things above 50% and certainly above 75% success levels. Sometimes looking at the probability of failure instantly tells us more than the one minus failure or success probability. Now, I wonder what it would produce if I asked it to create a fairly feature poor software defined radio.... If it does THAT well then it's approaching general utility rather closely.

Nonetheless I am sitting here in open mouthed astonishment.

{^o^}
